  "interpretation": "One seed-42 IID paired pilot comparing BadNet, Neurotoxin and PGD against FedAvg and the closed-loop relation-graph group-zero defense. All attacks share malicious clients 0-3, target label 7, 50% poisoning, tracked BatchNorm, 20 clients x 500 samples and the same initial model. Neurotoxin uses the local clean-gradient GradMask (keep ratio 0.25, per-layer). PGD uses parameter-scope projection with radius = 1.0 x the median client parameter-update norm of the previous round, broadcast by the server. Clean groups are shared across attacks; their ASR is the clean model's response to the reference trigger. The 2000-example training holdout and 1800 non-target ASR denominator are shared; the final test set is unused. Conclusions are limited to this seed and IID protocol."
